# Display: no overlapping UI

On the venue `/display` live screen, **UI objects must never overlap**.

## Hard rules

- Panels, docks, rails, tiles, timer, stats, logo, and the player board must not share screen space.
- Prefer **normal document flow** (grid/flex + gap). Do not use absolute/fixed positioning to stack chrome on top of other chrome.
- Do not use negative margins, negative gaps, or “board lift” tricks that pull one region into another.
- Gaps between regions are required; near-touching is OK, overlapping is not.
- The join/QR dock may sit upper-left above Round/Balls as a **stacked** column with clear gap — that is not overlap. It must not cover Round/Balls, tiles, timer, stats, or player cards.

## When changing layout

If a change would cause overlap, shrink or reflow in-flow content instead of layering with z-index.
